<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aitutaki</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aitutaki is an island in the southern Cook Islands, made up of a volcanic island and a ring of reef islets enclosing a large lagoon. Reached by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-bligh">William Bligh</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hms-bounty">Bounty</a> in 1789, it was the first of the Cook Islands to accept Christian missionaries, in 1821. It joined the federal government of the islands in the 1890s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aitutaki.jpg" alt="Aitutaki" width="320" height="347" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AST-01-039_Aituctaki_Atoll.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
